  "worked_solution": "Since $p(t)$ and $q(t)$ are orthogonal, their inner product must be zero.\n\nFirst, we compute the inner product using our definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u27e8p(t),q(t)\u27e9 & =p(1)q(1)+p(3)q(3) \\\\  & =(1-1)(k+3)+(3-1)(3k+3) \\\\  & =0+(6k+6) \\\\  & =6k+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set $\u27e8p(t),q(t)\u27e9=0$ and solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u27e8p(t),q(t)\u27e9 & =0 \\\\ 6k+6 & =0 \\\\ 6k & =-6 \\\\ k & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
